        "value": "Tokuyama Domain — the maru-marker opening this domain's entry, with its base assessment (honkoku) of 40,010 koku given in the parenthesis. Everything to the left of this marker is Tokuyama's; everything to its right is the tail of the preceding domain, Toyohashi. Read at single-character zoom, the last two glyphs are a plain cross 十 followed by 石 (厂 over 口), so the figure is 40,010 koku — the well-attested size of this Chōshū branch domain — and not the \"四萬十五\" recorded in the project's extracted dataset."
